.Dd April 30, 2026
.Dt EMU 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emu
.Nd FreeBSD kernel emulation framework management tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl o Ar format
.Op Fl g Ar gid
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
tool provides a unified command-line interface for managing emulated
instances of different architectures on
.Fx .
It supports both native virtualization via
.Xr bhyve 4
and pure software emulation for cross-architecture testing on
.Fx .
.Pp
The emulation framework allows safe testing of kernel modules without
risking system stability, enables testing of non-native architectures,
and provides isolated environments for kernel development.
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v , -verbose
Enable verbose output.
.It Fl q , -quiet
Suppress informational output.
.It Fl o , -output Ar format
Set output format.
.Ar format
can be:
.Bl -tag -width "text,json,tap,junit" -compact
.It text
Human-readable text output (default)
.It json
JSON output for machine parsing
.It tap
Test Anything Protocol output
.It junit
JUnit XML format for CI/CD integration
.El
.It Fl g , -emu-group Ar gid
Specify the emulation group ID for non-root operation.
The default group is the
.Pa emu
group.
.It Fl h , -help
Show help message.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
The following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar init
.Op Fl a Ar arch
.Op Fl c Ar level
.Op Fl m Ar size
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl s Ar sockets
.Op Fl v
.Xc
Initialize a new emulated instance.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl a Ar arch
Target architecture (amd64, i386, arm64, arm, powerpc, riscv)
.It Fl c Ar level
CPU compatibility level (1-3)
.It Fl m Ar size
Memory size (64M-64G, e.g., 512M, 2G)
.It Fl n Ar name
Instance name
.It Fl s Ar sockets
Number of CPU sockets (1-8)
.El
.Pp
Creates a new emulated instance with the specified configuration.
If no name is provided, one is auto-generated.
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar start
.Op Fl m Ar mode
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl v
.Xc
Start an emulated instance.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl m Ar mode
Execution mode (auto, bhyve, emulator)
.It Fl n Ar name
Instance name
.It Fl v
Verbose output
.El
.Pp
Starts the specified instance.
The execution mode is automatically selected based on host and target
architecture unless explicitly specified.
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar stop
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl t Ar timeout
.Op Fl v
.Xc
Stop an emulated instance.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl f
Force stop (SIGKILL)
.It Fl n Ar name
Instance name
.It Fl t Ar timeout
Shutdown timeout in seconds (default: 30)
.It Fl v
Verbose output
.El
.Pp
Gracefully stops the instance by sending SIGTERM first,
then SIGKILL if it does not stop within the timeout.
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar status
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar format
.Op Fl v
.Xc
Show status of an emulated instance.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl n Ar name
Instance name
.It Fl o Ar format
Output format (text, json)
.It Fl v
Verbose output
.El
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar list
.Op Fl a Ar arch
.Op Fl s Ar status
.Op Fl o Ar format
.Op Fl v
.Xc
List all emulated instances.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl a Ar arch
Filter by architecture
.It Fl s Ar status
Filter by status (running, stopped, paused, error)
.It Fl o Ar format
Output format (text, json)
.It Fl v
Verbose output
.El
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar destroy
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl v
.Xc
Destroy an emulated instance.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl f
Force destruction without confirmation
.It Fl n Ar name
Instance name
.It Fl v
Verbose output
.El
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar console
.Op Fl m Ar mode
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Xc
Display instance console output.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl m Ar mode
Console mode (tail, follow, dump)
.It Fl n Ar name
Instance name
.El
.Pp
Modes:
.Bl -tag -width "follow" -compact
.It tail
Show last 100 lines
.It follow
Continuously show new output (Ctrl+C to exit)
.It dump
Show complete console buffer
.El
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar load
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl v
.Ar module_path
.Xc
Load a kernel module into an emulated instance.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl n Ar name
Instance name
.It Fl v
Verbose output
.It Ar module_path
Path to kernel module (.ko file)
.El
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar unload
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl v
.Ar module_name
.Xc
Unload a kernel module from an emulated instance.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Fl n Ar name
Instance name
.It Fl v
Verbose output
.It Ar module_name
Name of the module to unload
.El
.It Xo
.Nm emu
.Ar stack
.Op Fl c Ar count
.Op Fl f Ar format
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl v
.Xc
Examine kernel stack trace from an emulated instance.
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
