.Sh ARCHITECTURES
The emulation framework supports the following architectures:
.Bl -tag -width "powerpc" -compact
.It amd64
x86-64 (64-bit)
.It i386
x86 (32-bit)
.It arm64
AArch64 (64-bit ARM)
.It arm
ARM (32-bit)
.It powerpc
PowerPC
.It riscv
RISC-V (64-bit)
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /etc/emu.conf
Default configuration file
.It Pa ~/.config/emu/
User-specific configuration directory
.It Pa /var/emu/
System-wide instance data directory
.It Pa /var/emu/instances/
Per-instance data directories
.It Pa /var/emu/blob-cache/
Downloaded firmware blob cache
.It Pa /var/emu/images/
Base disk images
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create and start an amd64 emulation instance:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ emu init -a amd64 -m 1G -n mytest
$ emu start -n mytest
.Ed
.Pp
Run tests in an emulated arm64 instance:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ emu init -a arm64 -n armtest
$ emu start -n armtest
$ emu load -n armtest /path/to/test_module.ko
$ emu test -n armtest
$ emu stop -n armtest
.Ed
.Pp
Create and restore a snapshot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ emu snapshot -n mytest -s before_experiment
$ emu load -n mytest /path/to/risky_module.ko
$ emu restore -n mytest -s before_experiment
.Ed
.Pp
List all instances in JSON format:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ emu list -o json
.Ed
.Pp
Manage firmware blobs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ emu blob list
$ emu blob download seabios
$ emu blob verify seabios
.Ed
.Pp
Verify emulation framework status:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ emu test -v
.Ed
.Pp
Load the emulation kernel module:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload emu_core
.Ed
.Sh HOST CONFIGURATION
This section describes how to configure the host system for secure emulation.
.Ss Loading the Kernel Module
Load the emulation kernel module at boot or manually:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /boot/loader.conf:
emu_core_load="YES"

# Or load manually:
# kldload emu_core
.Ed
.Pp
Check kernel module status:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldstat | grep emu_core
.Ed
.Ss Setting Securelevel
The securelevel controls the level of kernel hardening:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# To enable securelevel, add to /etc/rc.conf:
kern_securelevel_enable="YES"
kern_securelevel="1"
.Ed
.Pp
Available securelevels:
.Bl -tag -width "3" -compact
.It -1
Permanently insecure (never raise)
.It 0
Insecure mode (default for development)
.It 1
Secure mode (default for production)
.It 2
Highly secure
.It 3
Network-secure (maximum security)
.El
.Ss Enabling MAC Framework
To enable MAC enforcement:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /boot/loader.conf:
mac_veriexec_load="YES"

# Enable MAC policy
maclabel="root:secattr"

# See mac_seeotheruids(4) and mac_veriexec(4)
.Ed
.Ss Enabling Veriexec
To enable binary integrity verification:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Create /etc/veriexec manifest
# Format: path hash algorithm flags
/bin/sh sha256 abc123... flags

# Verify using veriexecctl
veriexecctl mode strict
.Ed
.Ss Configuring Resource Limits
Enable rctl resource limits:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /etc/rc.conf:
rctl_enable="YES"

# Create /etc/rctl.conf:
user:emu:maxproc=100
user:emu:memoryuse=4G
.Ed
.Ss Enabling Huge Pages
Configure huge pages for instance memory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /boot/loader.conf:
vm.pmap.pg_ps_enabled=1

# Or via sysctl:
sysctl vm.pmap.pg_ps_enabled=1
.Ed
.Ss Network Isolation
Configure isolated network for secure emulation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /etc/rc.conf:
cloned_interfaces="bridge0"
ifconfig_bridge0="addm emu0 10.0.0.1/24 up"
.Ed
.Ss Security Configuration Levels
The emulation framework supports multiple security levels:
.Ss Basic (Development)
For local development only:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf
securelevel=-1
mac_enforce=false
veriexec_check=false
audit_enabled=false
.Ed
.Ss Standard (Default)
For general use:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf
securelevel=1
mac_enforce=true
veriexec_check=true
audit_enabled=true
rctl_enabled=true
.Ed
.Ss High Security
For sensitive workloads:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf
securelevel=3
mac_enforce=true
veriexec_check=true
audit_enabled=true
audit_buffer_size=8192
rctl_enabled=true
network_isolation=true
.Ed
.Ss Maximum Security
For critical infrastructure:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf
securelevel=3
mac_enforce=true
veriexec_check=true
audit_enabled=true
audit_buffer_size=16384
rctl_enabled=true
network_isolation=true
huge_pages=true
memory_encryption=true
swap_encryption=true
.Ed
